\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(void)\b attachColorList:\b0 (NSColorList *)\i colorList\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Tells the color picker to attach the given \i colorList\i0 , if it isn\'27t already displaying the list. You never invoke this method; it\'27s invoked automatically by the NSColorPanel when its \b attachColorList:\b0  method is invoked. Since NSColorPanel\'27s list mode manages NSColorLists, this method need only be implemented by a custom color picker that manages NSColorLists itself. This method ordinarily doesn\'27t do anything, since NSColorPanel\'27s list mode manages NSColorLists.\
\fs14\
