\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(id)\b initWithPickerMask:\b0 (int)\i mask\
\fi0 \b \i0 colorPanel:\b0 (NSColorPanel *)\i owningColorPanel\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Notifies the color picker of the color panel\'27s mask and initializes the color picker. This method is sent by the NSColorPanel to all implementors of the color picking protocols when the application\'27s color panel is first initialized. In order for your color picker to receive this message, it must have a bundle in your application\'27s \'aaColorPickers\'ba directory (described in \'aaColor Picker Bundles\'ba in the Protocol Description). \
\fs14\
\fs28 \i mask\i0  is determined by the argument to the NSColorPanel method \b setPickerMask:\b0 . If no mask has been set, \i mask\i0  is NSColorPanelAllModesMask. If your color picker supports any additional modes, you should invoke the \b setPickerMask:\b0  method when your application initializes to notify the NSColorPanel class. The standard mask constants are:\
\fs14\
\pard \s63 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx5745 \tx6498 \tx7257 \tx9547 \tx10281 \tx11037 \f0 \b \fs28 Mode\tab Color Mask Constant\
\fs6\
\pard \s61 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx5745 \tx6497 \tx7257 \tx9547 \tx10281 \tx11037 \f1 \b0 \fs28 Grayscale-Alpha\tab NSColorPanelGrayModeMask\
\fi0 Red-Green-Blue\tab NSColorPanelRGBModeMask \
\fi0 Cyan-Yellow-Magenta-Black\tab NSColorPanelCMYKModeMask\
\fi0 Hue-Saturation-Brightness\tab NSColorPanelHSBModeMask\
\fi0 Custom palette\tab NSColorPanelCustomPaletteModeMask\
\fi0 Custom color list\tab NSColorPanelColorListModeMask \
\fi0 Color wheel\tab NSColorPanelWheelModeMask \
\fi0 All of the above\tab NSColorPanelAllModesMask \
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 This method should examine the mask and determine whether it supports any of the modes included there. You may also check the value in \i mask\i0  to enable or disable any subpickers or optional controls implemented by your color picker. Your color picker may also retain \i owningColorPanel\i0  in an instance variable for future communication with the color panel. \
\fs14\
\fs28 This method is provided to initialize your color picker; however, much of a color picker\'27s initialization may be done lazily through the NSColorPickingCustom protocol\'27s \b provideNewView:\b0  method. If your color picker responds to any of the modes represented in \i mask\i0 , it should perform its initialization and return \b self\b0 . Color pickers that do so have their buttons inserted in the color panel and continue to receive messages from the panel as the user manipulates it. If the color picker doesn\'27t respond to any of the modes represented in mask, it should do nothing and return \b nil\b0 . \
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \b +\'80setPickerMask:\b0  (NSColorPanel class)\
\fs14\
